<title>USA: Panaco buys Amoco properties for $51 million.</title>
<headline>Panaco buys Amoco properties for $51 million.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo.</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panaco Inc. said Tuesday it has agreed to buy Amoco Corp.'s stakes in 16 offshore blocks in the Gulf of Mexico for more than $51 million.</p>
<p>The purchase price includes $42.7 million in cash and two million shares of Panaco's common stock, the company said. Panaco traded at $4.25 a share, off 12.5 cents, on the Nasdaq market at midday.</p>
<p>Panaco said the blocks have an estimated reserve of 57 billion cubic feet of natural gas, and also include 2.5 million barrels of crude oil.</p>
</text>
